    "q-111503": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111503",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "The matrix $T$ is given below. Let ${t}_{1}$, ${t}_{2}$, and ${t}_{3}$ be the respective columns of $T.$\nDetermine if $B=\\text{{}{t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(T).$ \nIf that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${t}_{2}={x}_{1}{t}_{1}+{x}_{3}{t}_{3}.$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we reduce the matrix $T$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(T)$ is $\\{{t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $\\text{{}{t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\text{}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(T).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
